BAR Droid phone version of BAR's Vote interface (luaui/widgets/gui_vote_interface.lua), the panel an online game's
votes bring up (a team's resign, stop, forcestart): on the screen whole. BAR places it right of the top bar's middle,
under the top bar; upright on a phone the top bar is the screen's right half and the panel a third of the height wide,
so it ran past the right edge: only YES showed, the title, NO and the close button off the screen (dev phone, upright,
a "stop" vote, 2026-11-19). No wider than the screen and moved left until it fits, under the top bar as before.
Applied by the engine (BarDroidPhoneLuaDir) to BAR's file as LuaUI loads it; if a block finds no place, BAR's own file
runs.

@@@ find
		if WG.topbar ~= nil then
			local topbarArea = WG.topbar.GetPosition()
			xpos = mathFloor(topbarArea[1] + (width / 2) + widgetSpaceMargin + ((topbarArea[3] - topbarArea[1]) / 2))
			ypos = mathFloor(topbarArea[2] - widgetSpaceMargin - (height / 2))
		end
@@@ with
		if WG.topbar ~= nil then
			local topbarArea = WG.topbar.GetPosition()
			xpos = mathFloor(topbarArea[1] + (width / 2) + widgetSpaceMargin + ((topbarArea[3] - topbarArea[1]) / 2))
			ypos = mathFloor(topbarArea[2] - widgetSpaceMargin - (height / 2))
		end
		-- BAR Droid (phone): on the screen whole (upright it ran past the right edge, NO out of sight)
		do
			local droidM = math.max(2, widgetSpaceMargin or 2)
			if width > vsx - 2 * droidM then
				width = vsx - 2 * droidM
				buttonMargin = mathFloor(width / 32)
			end
			xpos = math.max(mathFloor(width / 2) + droidM, math.min(xpos, vsx - mathFloor(width / 2) - droidM))
		end
@@@ end
